# Whitelist, not a blocklist, and deliberately so.
#
# The gateway image is built from the repo root (the Dockerfile needs
# `gateway/requirements.txt` and `gateway/`), which means the default build
# context is this entire checkout: the .env, the live Instagram token in
# data/ig_token.json, the voice recordings, ~1.5 GB of models and venvs. A
# blocklist would protect that only for as long as nobody adds a file the list
# never anticipated, and the image is published to a public registry.
#
# So: ignore everything, then re-include exactly what the image needs. A
# careless `COPY . .` added later can then only ever copy gateway/.
*

!gateway/

# Re-included above as a directory, so the state that lives inside it has to be
# excluded again. None of this is in git either, but a developer who has run the
# service locally has all three sitting right next to the source.
gateway/covers/
gateway/state/
gateway/*.sqlite3
gateway/*.sqlite3-shm
gateway/*.sqlite3-wal
gateway/__pycache__/
gateway/**/__pycache__/

# The compose file and this Dockerfile describe the build; they are not part of
# the image.
gateway/docker-compose.yml
gateway/Dockerfile
